{
  "description": "The folder Claude Code files a working directory's conversations under, below <CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.claude>/projects/. Every UTF-16 code unit of the cwd that is not an ASCII letter or digit becomes '-'; a result longer than 200 units is cut to 200 and given '-' plus the base-36 absolute value of the cwd's Java-style String.hashCode (32-bit, over UTF-16 units). Asserted by the daemon's agent.transcripts locator; a client that computes the folder asserts the same file. The cwd is Claude Code's working directory with every symbolic link resolved (it takes realpathSync(process.cwd())), so a window opened through a link is filed under its target's folder; a '~' is expanded against the host's home before that, never by this rule. The cases below are the rule itself, applied to an already-resolved cwd.",
  "source": "Claude Code 2.1.288, bundled JS: k(e)=e.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g,\"-\"); iP(e){let n=k(e);if(n.length<=200)return n;return `${n.slice(0,200)}-${Math.abs(xee(e)).toString(36)}`}; xee(t){let e=0;for(let n=0;n<t.length;n++)e=(e<<5)-e+t.charCodeAt(n)|0;return e}. The cwd it is given: import{realpathSync as r}from\"fs\"; function jso(){...n=o(r(e))...} var qes=jso(), the default originalCwd that projects/<folder> is computed from. The expected values were produced by running those functions verbatim.",
  "max_units": 200,
